  "schema": "transfer-note-manager-endpoint-v1",
  "scope": "Shared functional NoteManager insertion source recurrence and its actual note/volume callback installation into the qualified raw effect model. SCT error retains its actual callback cache before any additional pending-object write. Success derives the returned position and exact append to post-SCT pending payloads; semantic note event follows success. Native/durability/SCT semantic correspondence, atomic evidence refresh and full Transfer remain open. Success derives the actual SCT return position, current post-SCT pending getter, exact append tuple and one pending object update. Additional update frames post-SCT verifiable/NV/events/other objects, not original input cache. Note callback SCT failure retains its actual failure cache and suppresses semantic note-created and all later outputs; successful note preserves internal SCT events then appends one semantic event. Ordinary payload failure occurs after two marker writes and retains its actual failed SCT cache; those earlier markers are not asserted to survive an arbitrary callback overwrite. All underlying SCT/codec/ownership/alias/durability interfaces remain explicit.",
  "toolchain_bytes_in_archive": 0
}
